  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/limnopilos-naiyanetri/",
      "html": "<p>Described in 1991, Limnopilos naiyanetri Chuang &amp; Ng, has only just been discovered by the hobby.</p><ul><li>Origin: Thailand</li><li>Available size: 0.3–0.5 cm</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/limnopilos-naiyanetri/",
      "html": "<p>Crabs are found in pure freshwater in the roots of floating vegetation, i.e. water hyacinth (Eichornia crassipes) and fine-leaved aquatic plants along the riparian zone (river banks). They have hairy bodies and appendages which collect mud and dirt and may function to trap food particles.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/limnopilos-naiyanetri/",
      "html": "<p>Suitable for nano tanks, and is the first crab species available which has attributes suitable for such.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/limnopilos-naiyanetri/",
      "html": "<p>They are not carnivorous, and behave like Caridina shrimps in their scavenging behaviours, where care and feeding are probably the same.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/limnopilos-naiyanetri/",
      "html": "<p>In such tanks they will stay closely associated with mosses and fine-leaved plants.</p>"
    }
  ],
